{
 "schema_version": 1,
 "spec_id": "var-gs_vy-gvytls-v1",
 "title": "GS21 gvytl with the exposure ladder MIRRORED: six level-exposure types gs_bv -0.10, -0.05, -0.015, 0.015, 0.05, 0.10 (E[b] = 0, level-compensated) x three fixed coupons 0.15 / 0.40 / 0.70 per unit capital (capital structure fixed for life), eighteen types of equal share, price 2.5",
 "question": "Does GS21 hide a signed exposure type once the firm cannot choose its coupon? gvy25s (signed types, GS21's own debt dynamics) kept 88% of SR_max in the linear ceiling and gave no gap; vyg25s (KP14, the firm chooses nothing) gave room 201% and +0.181. Here only investment and default remain as choices that could reveal the sign.",
 "notes": "WHY (2026-10-28, user request). The signed-type mechanism that works in KP14 fails in GS21 (gvy25s) and is weak in BGN (bvychs). The ordering of the three rooms (201% / 20% / 11%) is the ordering of how much the firm decides, and GS21's largest decision is its coupon. This economy removes that decision: gvytl's chassis (gs_fixcs 1, xi 0, three coupon types drawn at birth independently of the exposure type) with the exposure ladder mirrored exactly as gvy25s mirrors gvy25. The level compensation gs_ashift = -1.2 log W(gs_bv) is derived per stage by gs_solve_vy.py (gvy25s: -0.580 at -0.10, +0.538 at +0.10; the coupon does not enter W). The simulator reads each type's coupon from its solution file (gs_blo) and checks GS_VY_BV against the solves.\n\nNOTE on the benchmark: the linear ceiling (lin_rank, constant weights) and the fair linear estimator do NOT condition on y; DKKM's random features see rf_stand and y_stand. Room is constant-weight on both sides.\n\nPRECOMMITMENT STATUS: precommitted=false; ids filled from the Quest build log by the solve script before any seed runs.\n\nPREDICTION (2026-10-28): room 15-25% of the linear ceiling (gvy25s 11%, gvytl's unsigned chassis for comparison), fair gap +0.01 to +0.03. FALSIFIED as 'the coupon choice is what reveals the sign' if room stays at or below gvy25s's 11%; if room exceeds 50% the mechanism is KP14's and investment timing does not reveal the sign.",
 "lineage": {
  "parent_spec": "var-gs_vy-gvytl-v1",
  "changes": [
   "exposure ladder gs_bv [0.015, 0.05, 0.10] -> mirrored [-0.10, -0.05, -0.015, 0.015, 0.05, 0.10], E[b] = 0 (as gvy25s mirrors gvy25)",
   "nine types -> eighteen (six exposures x three fixed coupons 0.15 / 0.40 / 0.70), equal shares; eighteen solves sol_gvytlsa..r",
   "gs_fixcs 1, xi 0, bv_comp 1.2, gamma_v 2.5, kappa_y 0.35, NY 9, y_mult 2.5 unchanged"
  ]
 },
